  "description": "Yalla!! V2 Öhlins Rolling Chassis\nThe RAAW Yalla!! V2 is our answer to riders who want it all: proven performance, more versatility, and that unmistakable Yalla! feeling. Born on the legendary slopes of Champéry and refined through countless laps on race tracks and bike parks alike, the V2 builds on everything we loved about the original—just better. We kept the trusted geometry and suspension kinematics but added new features like adjustable, UDH-compatible dropouts and the option to run 29” or MX setups. Whether you’re chasing podiums or weekend thrills, the Yalla! V2 is built to go fast, take hits, and keep going—again and again.\nWith the Rolling Chassis Kit we offer you a high-quality foundation for your individual build. You'll be ready to go in no time with the included component package yet still have plenty of room to create your own personal bike masterpiece – who wants an off the shelf build anyway?\nWe provide a Öhlins DH38 m.1 Air TTX18 fork with the frame, which you can combine with your preferred Fox or Öhlins shock at the rear.\nFor the cockpit, we rely on OneUp Components and offer you the DH stem and the carbon handlebar with either 20 mm or 35 mm rise, so you can feel comfortable from the get go. Ergon’s GDH Team grips and SM Downhill saddle round out the touch points.\nThe Rolling Chassis is topped off with the optional DT Swiss FR1500 wheels, equipped with a Maxxis Assegai and Minion DHR2 combination, both in their finest DH casing and 3C MaxxGrip rubber. This combination is our current go-to in almost all conditions.\nTo get you off to a good start in building your new bike, we've already pressed the headset cups into the frame and mounted the crown race on the fork. The tubeless tape and valves are also installed, you’ll just need to add in some sealant. The rest of the components are ready for you to assemble – this way you can truly experience the build process from the ground up and get to know your new bike and all its technical details. But you’re never on your own, as our support is always there if you need help building and can’t find the answer you’re after in our extensive knowledge base.",
